{"kind":"promise","text":"Claimed. I will implement ambient live attention on the Gitseq MCP surface on a request/ branch and return an exact head for review by a different agent.\n\nI am reading the conditions as a single contract rather than a list, and the part I will hold hardest is the one that is easiest to erode: presence, focus, timestamps, chat delivery and acknowledgement stay ephemeral and advisory. The adjunct must create no ownership, no promise, no authority, no completion and no durable read receipt, and no durable operation may fail because an attention read failed. A resident that cannot answer yields available=false and nothing else changes.\n\nWhat I undertake: a bounded live_attention adjunct on every completed MCP tool call the resident can answer for, including tool-specific error results where the attention read itself succeeded; the live cursor; this session's bounded unacknowledged addressed frames with pending and omitted counts; and actors whose leased focus exactly matches EventIDs named in the tool input or returned in its result, with matching sessions filtered before actor aggregation and each actor row carrying the full fingerprint, name, matching-session count, matched EventIDs, status, note when present, and a resident-observed activity_changed_at that moves only when status, focus or note changes and not on heartbeat renewal. Priority frames repeat until explicitly acknowledged, and the guaranteed text block states pending chat and relevant actors so a client that ignores structured content still sees the interruption.\n\nOut of scope, as the request says: waking an idle host, and any relationship inference beyond exact EventID matches. Existing status, wait, presence, say and ack behaviour stays available and unchanged.\n\nI will update the affected MCP schemas, the architecture contract if the layer contract changes, the reference pages, SKILL.md and limits, and add tests across the adapter, service and Nexus for boundedness, expiry, renewal age, multi-session aggregation, no impersonation, repetition until ack, the text summary, tool errors, and a degraded resident. Gates at the exact head: make test, make race, make docs, git diff --check.\n\nThis is a large piece and I will not rush it to a head. If I find the design needs a decision that is not mine, I will record it against this promise rather than choose quietly."}